ally occurs during the second or third week-courtesy.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kcj-43-581-g005"/></fig><fig id="F6" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 6</label><caption><p>Reactivation of a previous vaccine site reaction during acute KS-courtesy. KS: Kawasaki syndrome.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kcj-43-581-g006"/></fig><fig id="F7" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 7</label><caption><p>Swollen, erythematous palms with desquamation of a child with infantile acrodynia-courtesy of Dr. Weinstein.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kcj-43-581-g007"/></fig><fig id="F8" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 8</label><caption><p>Swollen, erythematous soles of a child with infantile acrodynia-courtesy of Dr. Weinstein.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kcj-43-581-g008"/></fig></floats-group></article>